【December 29 Market News and Data Analysis】
1. Christmas holiday institutions exit, spot #BTC  ETF net outflow of $782 million;
2. #solana  publishes 2025 annual summary: DEX trading volume exceeds $1.7 trillion this year, total ETF scale exceeds $766 million;
3. This week's unlocking data overview: #hype , ZORA, #sui , etc. will welcome a large one-time token unlock;
4. Analysis: Market undercurrents surge, BTC and #ETH  may face a trend shift.

Data shows that during Christmas week, the Bitcoin spot ETF listed in the U.S. experienced significant capital outflow, with a cumulative net outflow of about $780 million, among which the highest single-day net outflow reached $276 million. BlackRock's IBIT saw an outflow of nearly $190 million that day, Fidelity's FBTC about $74 million, while Grayscale's GBTC continued to have small redemptions. As a result, the overall asset scale of ETFs dropped from about $120 billion at the beginning of the year to around $113.5 billion. It's worth noting that despite continuous capital withdrawal, the Bitcoin spot price remains around $87,000, suggesting that this round of outflow is more likely a routine operation for year-end asset rebalancing and reduced holiday liquidity, rather than panic selling.
From the market structure perspective, the continuous net outflow of ETF funds has lasted for six trading days, totaling over $1.1 billion, forming the longest capital withdrawal cycle since this autumn. At the same time, the derivatives market shows signals that are completely different from the spot ETFs: volatility narrows, leverage usage remains high, and stablecoin trading does not synchronize with futures positions. On the technical front, Bitcoin's RSI is about 43% (bullish) while the stochastic indicator is about 30% (bearish), with approximately 4.5% distance to trigger a trend reversal, short-term key support is around $88,400, if it can hold, it is expected to rebound in January. Overall, if capital re-enters the ETF at the beginning of the year, it may provide new support for Bitcoin prices, pushing the market from the current weak range to a moderate upward trend.
